# Web image size

Every photograph or image added under `assets/images/photography/` — gallery
photos, essay images and field note images — must be a web copy:

- Long edge at most **2000px** (never upscale), sRGB, JPEG.
- File size **under 1 MB**. If a 2000px copy is still larger, lower the JPEG
  quality (88 → 82 → 76) until it fits.
- Never commit the full-size export, RAW files or print masters. Read the
  user's export from its original location and write only the resized copy
  into the repo; leave the original untouched.

Do this before watermarking (the watermark scales with the image, and files
are only marked once), then run the variants:

```bash
magick "<export>.jpg" -colorspace sRGB -resize '2000x2000>' -quality 88 \
  assets/images/photography/<folder>/<file>.jpg
magick identify -format '%wx%h %b\n' assets/images/photography/<folder>/<file>.jpg
./scripts/watermark-photos assets/images/photography/<folder>
./scripts/build-image-variants
```

If images already in the repo are too large and already watermarked, resize
from an unwatermarked original, not from the marked file, so the mark isn't
applied twice.
